                <pb facs="0410" n="390" xml:id="pg390"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">From British Legation.</hi></head>
                <note rend="inline"><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum.—Case of the Mont
                    Blanc.</hi></note>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-08-10"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >August</hi> 10, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>In a note dated the 16th of July Lord Lyons observed that on being informed by
                    Mr. Seward that directions to proceed to the assessment of damages in this case
                    would be given to Rear-Admiral Bailey, he would, on his part, take care that
                    proper directions should be sent to Mr. Vice-Consul Butterfield.</p>
                <p>Lord Lyons is waiting for this information before taking any further steps.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
